M.add(26641,"Step after invoicing lists lines-added services; already-complete excluded",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["Invoice a work order that added the lines of one or more services.","Confirm the step lists each such service, ticked by default, with its reason (e.g. 'Lines added from PM-A').","Untick one and confirm it does not reset and stays due.",
  "Confirm a service already reset by Mark complete is not listed, and a service whose schedule was removed while the work order was open is not listed and does not reset."],
 ["The step after invoicing lists every service whose lines were added on this work order, each ticked by default and can be unticked, with its reason (e.g. 'Lines added from PM-A').",
  "An unticked service does not reset and stays due.",
  "A service already reset by Mark complete is not listed (a service resets once); a service whose schedule was removed while the work order was open is not listed and does not reset."],
 [("S18-R8","The step after invoicing lists every service whose lines were added on this work order, each ticked by default and can be unticked, with its reason, for example Lines added from PM-A. An unticked service does not reset and stays due. A service already reset by Mark complete is not listed: a service resets once"),
  ("S18-R18","A service whose schedule was removed from the asset while its work order was open is not listed in the step after invoicing and does not reset")])
M.add(26641,"A closed line stamps its close date; a service completes via any of five paths",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["Close a line and confirm it stamps the date it closed, visible on the work order and distinct from the invoice date.","Confirm a service added by canned lines completes when every line it added completes, and a service marked complete without lines completes when it is marked.",
  "Confirm line completion counts via any of the five paths: completing the line, the bulk action bar, creating an invoice, clocking out, and review."],
 ["Each closed line stamps the date it closed, visible on the work order and distinct from the invoice date.",
  "A service added by its canned lines completes when every line it added completes; a service marked complete without lines completes when it is marked.",
  "Line completion counts by any of the five paths: completing the line, the bulk action bar, creating an invoice, clocking out, and review."],
 [("S18-R9","Each closed line will stamp the date it closed, visible on the work order and distinct from the invoice date"),
  ("S18-R10","A service added by its canned lines completes when every line it added completes. A service marked complete without lines completes when it is marked. The spec means line completion by any of the five paths that reach it: completing the line, the bulk action bar, creating an invoice, clocking out, and review")])
M.add(26641,"Completion records where it happened and travels across the organization",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["Complete a service at one location (including 'Completed elsewhere' naming another shop).","Confirm the completion records where it happened.","At another location, confirm the unit's schedule has advanced.","Confirm the system does not try to detect work done elsewhere."],
 ["Completion records where it happened, including another shop.",
  "Completion travels across the organization: a unit serviced at one location advances what another location tracks.",
  "The system cannot detect work done elsewhere and does not try; the reminder is what prompts the customer to mention it."],
 [("S18-R11","Completion will record where it happened, including another shop"),
  ("S18-R12","Completion travels across the organization. A unit serviced at one location advances what another location tracks"),
  ("S18-E5","The system cannot detect work done elsewhere and does not try. The reminder is what prompts the customer to mention it")])
M.add(26641,"Invoicing step: editable date, Confirm dates, certificates, skippable",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["In the step after invoicing, confirm the proposed date is editable and names the day the work was done, with next due following it.","Use Confirm dates to accept every proposal in one action; confirm closing the step without touching it accepts every proposal too.",
  "Confirm a Compliance certificates section appears for every compliance service on the work order.","Confirm the step appears only where a maintenance service was completed, never on an ordinary work order, and nothing blocks closing the work order."],
 ["The proposed date is editable and names the day the work was done; the next due follows from it and updates as it changes.",
  "Confirm dates accepts every proposed date in one action; closing the step without touching it accepts every proposal too, and the step is skippable (nothing blocks closing the work order).",
  "The step carries a Compliance certificates section for every compliance service on the work order (one record per inspection: type, number, Start date, End date and term), and it is optional.",
  "The step appears only where a maintenance service was completed; it never appears on an ordinary work order."],
 [("S18-R13","Where a work order added the lines of one or more maintenance services, invoicing it shows each of those services with the date its cycle counts from. The date proposed is when that service's own lines were all closed, which S18-R9 stamps, and the invoice date only where there is nothing better. Every path that closes a line stamps that date: completing the line, the bulk action bar, creating an invoice, clocking out and review. Where a path leaves no date, the invoice date is proposed"),
  ("S18-R14","The proposed date is editable and names the day the work was done. The next due follows from it through the service's own interval and updates as it changes, so a shop invoicing weeks late resets from the work rather than from the paperwork"),
  ("S18-R15","Accepting every proposed date is one action, Confirm dates. A shop that invoices on the day of the work passes through without touching it, and closing the step without touching it accepts every proposal too, per S18-N5"),
  ("S18-R16","The same step carries a Compliance certificates section for every compliance service on this work order, one record per inspection: type, number, Start date, End date and term, where Start date plus the term fills End date per S8-R10. The section is optional"),
  ("S18-N5","The step appears only where a maintenance service was completed. It never appears on an ordinary work order, and leaving without touching it accepts every proposal, on the same rule as S18-N1"),
  ("S18-N6","Completing a work order shows no maintenance step. Everything happens in the step after invoicing"),
  ("S18-N1","The completion step is skippable. Nothing blocks closing a work order")])
M.add(26641,"Mark complete toast + Undo; the row reads Completed and leaves the worklist",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["Mark complete a service.","Read the toast and use Undo.","Read the row afterwards and its menu.","Check the worklist."],
 ["After Mark complete a toast reads 'PM-A marked complete · next due counts from 2 Oct 2026', with Undo.",
  "The row reads 'Completed · next due counts from 2 Oct 2026', and its menu offers Undo complete until the service's next cycle moves again.",
  "On the worklist the row leaves the list."],
 [("S18-R17","After Mark complete a toast reads PM-A marked complete · next due counts from 2 Oct 2026, with Undo. The row reads Completed · next due counts from 2 Oct 2026, and its menu offers Undo complete until the service's next cycle moves again. On the worklist the row leaves the list")])
M.add(26641,"Completion works with no canned line, and nothing scolds a freeform shop",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["Complete a service on a work order whose lines were all typed freeform (no canned line anywhere).","Confirm completion works and nothing warns or scolds."],
 ["Completion works with no canned line involved anywhere (many shops type every line freeform).",
  "Nothing scolds - a shop typing freeform is not doing anything wrong."],
 [("S18-N3","Completion must work with no canned line involved anywhere, because many shops type every line freeform"),
  ("S18-N4","Nothing scolds. A shop typing freeform is not doing anything wrong")])
M.add(26641,"Edge: early completion, reversal/void, and serviced-now-invoiced-later",S,L,P,
 p18,
 ["Complete a compliance service months early and confirm nothing warns or confirms.","Where a cycle fell back to the invoice date, reverse and re-invoice and confirm it recalculates from the new invoice (unless a later completion superseded it).",
  "Void an invoice (credit memo) and confirm the original date is left intact.","Mark complete on Monday a truck invoiced three weeks later and confirm the next cycle counts from Monday and the worklist shows nothing due in between."],
 ["Early completion is normal: fleets move compliance work months earlier and nothing warns or confirms.",
  "Where a cycle fell back to the invoice date, reversing and re-invoicing recalculates it from the new invoice, unless a later completion has already superseded it.",
  "A voided invoice is not a case: reversal is a credit memo and leaves the original date intact.",
  "A truck serviced Monday and invoiced three weeks later is marked complete on Monday and counts its next cycle from Monday; the worklist shows nothing due in between and invoicing later changes nothing."],
 [("S18-E1","Early completion is normal. Fleets move compliance work months earlier to fit a slow season, and nothing warns or confirms"),
  ("S18-E2","Where a cycle fell back to the invoice date per S18-R13, reversing and re-invoicing the work order recalculates it from the new invoice, unless a later completion has already superseded it"),
  ("S18-E3","A voided invoice is not a case. Reversal is a credit memo and leaves the original date intact"),
  ("S18-E8","A truck serviced on Monday and invoiced three weeks later is marked complete on Monday and counts its next cycle from Monday. The worklist shows nothing due for it in between, and invoicing later changes nothing")])
